    "text": "A small smooth disc of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> moving with an initial velocity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></math> along the positive <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>-axis collided with a big disc of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> which was initially at rest with its centre at origin as shown in the figure. If the coefficient of restitution is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>, then the velocity of the larger disc after the collision is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0021021_Question_1.jpg\" style=\"width: 254px; height: 184px;\" />",
